{"name":"Fatal Fury","hex":"#da321c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fatal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Proceeding from, or appointed by, fate or destiny.","Foreboding death or great disaster."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fatality; an event that leads to death.","A fatal error; a failure that causes a program to terminate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fatal"},{"term":"fury","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Extreme anger.","Strength or violence in action."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thief."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fury"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fatal Fury","blocks":[{"text":"Fatal Fury, known as Garō Densetsu  in Japan, is a fighting game series developed by SNK, first released on SNK's Neo Geo system. Similar to other games from the genre, the franchise involves rounds where the player is given access to both combos and special techniques needed to defeat enemies. The franchise was started by Fatal Fury: King of Fighters (1991), and has come to include several spin-offs and anime adaptations."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b1/Fatalfurylogo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatal_Fury"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7c/NEOGEO_Fatal_Fury_-_King_of_Fighters_%28Gar%C5%8D_Densetsu_-_Shukumei_no_Tatakai%29.png/250px-NEOGEO_Fatal_Fury_-_King_of_Fighters_%28Gar%C5%8D_Densetsu_-_Shukumei_no_Tatakai%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7c/NEOGEO_Fatal_Fury_-_King_of_Fighters_%28Gar%C5%8D_Densetsu_-_Shukumei_no_Tatakai%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7c/NEOGEO_Fatal_Fury_-_King_of_Fighters_%28Gar%C5%8D_Densetsu